            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous closure of a coronary aneurysm with a vein-coated stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysm is a rare but recognized complication following percutaneous intervention. We report the formation of such an aneurysm after recanalization with Excimer laser wire of a chronic totally occluded left anterior descending coronary artery and stent implantation and its subsequent treatment using an autologous vein graft-coated stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
